TEXT -96 688 Left 2 !.ac dec 20 1 10G
TEXT -96 744 Left 2 ;Two-stage Miller op-amp: the 5T OTA (M1-M5, bias M8, IB = 10 uA) drives the PMOS common-source stage M6 with the sink M7 (60 uA).\nGBW = gm1 / (2 pi C1), second pole near gm6 / (2 pi CL), right-half-plane zero at gm6 / (2 pi C1); more gm6 means more phase margin.\nLFB closes the loop at DC and CFB opens it for AC, so the run gives the open-loop gain with the output biased at 0.7 V.
